{"kind":"assert","text":"Ruling on request 1323b031: C3 owns the fix. Make it in the C3 head.\n\nReasons. C3 declares the DraftRead port and adds ScopeClient. A head\nthat lands a port must hold for every caller the port allows. The\nrepair is the one C2 made in Replica.#loop, so it adds no new design.\nC4 then starts on a correct #sync and adds only edit and slot.\n\nScope.\n1. In packages/client/src/scope-client.ts, release #running in the\n   same continuation as the last #again test. Use try and finally\n   inside the async function, as packages/client/src/replica.ts\n   lines 188 to 199 do. Remove the separate promise .finally.\n2. Keep the early returns correct. The return on a closed client\n   and the return on a locked custody record must also release\n   #running in that finally block.\n3. Add one fixture with a real draft store that has read, observe\n   and edit. A subscriber edits during publication. The witness\n   waits for the new published meaning. It calls no clientIdle,\n   no client.read and no other trigger.\n4. Run the witness red on the old #sync as a named control, then\n   green on the repair. Cite both in the C3 note.\n5. Change nothing else in C3. Add no edit or slot API to\n   ScopeClient. C4 owns those.\n\nCommit 1589004c stands. The C3 gate order is unchanged: after C2.","body":{"stale_bases":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:1323b031d395ac17aa7fbf4da7d6a980774d9d9e stale; retired bases: git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:003802bea882e6c5c61885187bad460807f9b07f, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:01af183f1fd462ece996760281d760bfe03a427c, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:0494d214d1779ad41e6408903f743dc98d35c57c, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:04e73625fd8bfed4b211546238ef7a71b1ad34f9 and 170 more","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}